            <ArticleTitle>Addressing the needs of treating congenital heart disease: The influence of deficient retro-aortic rim on technical success and early adverse events following device closure of secundum atrial septal defects: An analysis of the IMPACT registry®.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>112-113</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.26891</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For secundum ASD, a deficient retro-aortic rim is common (40% of cases) However, the deficient retro-aortic rim had no effect on ASD device placement success or immediate outcome The IMPACT Registry does not track long-term outcome, so there is no information provided about long-term complications, such as erosion.</AbstractText>
